{"availability":"available","full":"rn-collins/entheogen-atlas","name":"entheogen-atlas","description":"A complete research atlas of entheogenic substances: archaeology, neuroscience, legal history, phenomenology, and religious use — mapped across 60,000 years.","category":"Other","language":"HTML","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-01T08:20:23Z","updated":"2026-10-17T05:48:25Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://entheogen-atlas.vercel.app","topics":["psychedelics","reference","research","rn-collins","static-site","vercel"],"demo":"https://entheogen-atlas.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T15:43:45.419Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T15:43:45.419Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T15:43:45.419Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T07:59:59.907Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-18T15:43:45.419Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A research atlas of entheogenic substances: archaeology, neuroscience, legal history, phenomenology and religious use, anchored on the oldest chemically confirmed use of a psychedelic — peyote from Shumla Cave, radiocarbon dated to 3780–3660 cal BC and shown by GC-MS to contain mescaline, about 5,700 years ago.","Older claims are listed where they are serious, and separated from the confirmed record by an explicit evidence ladder rather than merged into a single headline figure. The 60,000-year Shanidar Cave claim that circulates widely is carried as a contested claim, not as evidence: the pollen it rests on is now attributed to burrowing rodents, and the assemblage contains no entheogen."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rn-collins/entheogen-atlas/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"13db2c843d0afec3b64d4c5e570d480d81c1efcbfa3480d2ec141ad435e96e08","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T08:00:00.022Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T08:00:00.022Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A research atlas of en